            <ArticleTitle>ATP receptors in sickness, pain and death.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extracellular ATP elicits biological responses ranging from cell death to synaptic transmission. Recent gene-cloning efforts have uncovered a family of cell-surface ATP receptors, which are potential targets for the development of novel drugs to treat airway and cardiovascular diseases, inflammation and pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
